{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>וְאִם נֶפֶשׁ וגו׳.</b> It says <b>וְאִם</b> with a vav to add to the first matter what He traced from the laws in this parashah, that there is in them no contrariness to what is stated before them." "<b>מֵעַם הָאָרֶץ.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory (Horayot 11a) expounded it to exclude the anointed priest in his unwitting sin without concealment [of the matter], that he does not bring even a she-goat. Also the mem of ״מֵעַם״ they said excludes the prince in a case where he ate half an olive-bulk as a commoner and half an olive-bulk as king, that he does not bring a ewe. Meaning: first they expound ״עַם הָאָרֶץ״ — which is to exclude the great and distinguished one among them, namely the anointed priest, and this exposition would have been derived even if it had said ״בְּעַם הָאָרֶץ״; and from His saying ״מֵעַם״ He went back and separated off also a portion of the commoner — such as a commoner who ate half an olive-bulk and was then appointed and completed it, that he does not bring." "<b>בַּעֲשׂוֹתָהּ.</b> It was not necessary to say it, and they expounded from it in Torat Kohanim a limitation and an expansion: Limitation — that if he acted on the basis of a ruling of the court he is exempt, for one might have thought that what the verse fixed the bull of the congregation for applies only to the court, which was the cause in their ruling for the sin, but the ones who act according to their law stand to bring a ewe or a she-goat; it teaches us that it is specifically one who relies on himself. Expansion — that if he relied on the court, meaning that the court ruled and he acted according to their word, if he knew that they erred he is not exempt by virtue of their ruling and is obligated in a she-goat or a ewe, even though the court brings the bull of the sin-offering according to its law. The expansion is alluded to in the word ״בַּעֲשׂוֹת,״ and the limitation in the precise form ״בַּעֲשׂוֹתָהּ״ — implying: in doing it [specifically] and not another; and through this you will understand the two baraitot in Torat Kohanim correctly."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:53:17.087026679Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}